<urn:beads-cache:finding:RSH-001> triage:id "RSH-001" ; triage:sprint "c-1" ; triage:severity "critical" ; triage:location "crates/bd-cache-sync/src/cron.rs:198" ; triage:source "qa-3 owning reviewer fenced JSON" ; triage:status "open" ; triage:record "{\"carry_forward_from\": \"qa-2 specialist output; unchanged production source, still open\", \"evidence\": \"OPEN at assigned HEAD: crates/bd-cache-sync/src/cron.rs:198 still constructs worker.shutdown(now + shutdown_timeout), :202 awaits it, :214 awaits that same future after a hurried stop, and :217-225 calls the ordinary expiry kill/callback only after shutdown returns. Cargo.toml:36 and Cargo.lock:1153-1154 remain published sc-cron exactly 0.1.1. Its actual installed registry source /Users/randlee/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/sc-cron-0.1.1/src/scheduler.rs:912-931 still times out then awaits task without abort; worker.rs:539-550 still awaits an uncancelled blocking store call. Thus the original contended reload/persistence occurrence remains. No workaround or baseline change was introduced. The sprint explicitly records this blocker at docs/plans/phase-c/sprint-c-1-runtime-migration.md:511 and :540-545.\", \"file\": \"crates/bd-cache-sync/src/cron.rs\", \"id\": \"RSH-001\", \"issue\": \"The migrated shutdown call no longer enforces the existing bounded stop contract. Published sc-cron 0.1.1 waits for its worker even after the handle deadline. A worker awaiting a contended shared-store call can therefore keep cron_run_hurried beyond T and its documented 2*T total bound; on the ordinary expiry path the bd-kill callback is itself delayed until that wait ends. A second signal also awaits the same unresolved shutdown future at line 211. This violates REQ-BDC-0730 and the preserved REQ-CRON-0012 semantics.\", \"line\": 198, \"recommendation\": \"Resolve the mismatch upstream and qualify an approved bounded-shutdown contract before accepting the migration. Ensure expiry triggers kill immediately and cleanup finishes within the existing absolute shutdown bound, including a worker blocked in reload/persistence. Do not fork the scheduler or replace the bound with an async timeout that leaves detached ownership behind.\", \"reviewer\": \"rust-service-hardening-agent\", \"severity\": \"critical\", \"topic\": \"graceful_shutdown\"}" .

